            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for a fox, then the Bengali for a wolf."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: দল",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দল — dôl — \"a team, a group\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দল (dôl) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from dala, \"party, band\" (CDIAL 6215). CDIAL lists Bengali dal, \"company\", and reports Burrow's view that the word is Dravidian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
